1
00:00:03,347 --> 00:00:04,817
SHELDON:
Leonard...

2
00:00:04,815 --> 00:00:06,315
(Sheldon:)I've got terrible news.

3
00:00:06,317 --> 00:00:07,187
(Leonard:)What's going on?

4
00:00:07,184 --> 00:00:08,654
(Sheldon:)Before I tell you,

5
00:00:08,652 --> 00:00:11,122
(Sheldon:)perhaps I should
soften the blow.

6
00:00:11,121 --> 00:00:15,421
Your face
is pleasingly symmetrical.

7
00:00:15,426 --> 00:00:17,626
(Leonard:)Just tell me.

8
00:00:17,628 --> 00:00:19,758
(Sheldon:)A Swedish team of physicists

9
00:00:19,763 --> 00:00:22,633
(Sheldon:)is trying to scoop our super-
fluid vortex experiment.

10
00:00:22,633 --> 00:00:24,733
(Leonard:)Oh, well, that kind of stinks.

11
00:00:24,735 --> 00:00:26,405
“That kind of stinks”?

12
00:00:26,403 --> 00:00:28,203
(Sheldon:)Why aren't you more upset?

13
00:00:28,205 --> 00:00:29,805
(Sheldon:)Did I soften the blow too much?

14
00:00:29,807 --> 00:00:34,247
(Sheldon:)Because this here is more
like a Picasso painting.

15
00:00:34,245 --> 00:00:36,615
(Leonard:)What are we going to do?

16
00:00:36,614 --> 00:00:38,114
(Sheldon:)Perform the experiment
immediately.

17
00:00:38,115 --> 00:00:40,015
(Leonard:)I'd love to,
but we need liquid helium

18
00:00:40,017 --> 00:00:42,547
(Leonard:)and our shipment's
on back order for a month.

19
00:00:42,553 --> 00:00:44,623
(Sheldon:)A month? What?
Are you kidding me?

20
00:00:44,622 --> 00:00:47,492
(Sheldon:)That would have been a good time
for you to soften the blow.

21
00:00:47,491 --> 00:00:50,931
(Leonard:)That shirt brings out
the blue in your eyes.

22
00:00:50,928 --> 00:00:53,328
(Sheldon:)Thank you.
Aren't you sweet.

23
00:00:53,330 --> 00:00:55,360
(Leonard:)Let's go check to see
if the university

24
00:00:55,366 --> 00:00:57,596
(Leonard:)has any helium in reserve.

25
00:00:57,601 --> 00:01:02,021
(Sheldon:)Did you know that I almost
didn't wear this shirt today?

